-- title:
--   Wild–tame–unramified chain with cyclic tame and top steps
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a group and $q$ a prime. Let $U, W \le G$ be normal subgroups with $U$ of finite index and $U \le W$, such that every $w \in W$ satisfies $w^{q^{a}} \in U$ for some natural number $a$ (so $W/U$ has $q$-power exponent). Let $t, \varphi \in G$ be elements with $(t^{q})^{-1}\,(\varphi t \varphi^{-1}) \in W$, i.e. $\varphi t \varphi^{-1} \equiv t^{q}$ modulo $W$, and suppose that for every $g \in G$ there is a natural number $n$ with $(\varphi^{n})^{-1} g$ lying in the subgroup generated by $t$ together with $W$, so that $G = \bigcup_{n \ge 0} \varphi^{n}\,\langle t\rangle W$. Let further $H \le S$ be subgroups with $U \le H$ and with $H$ normal in $S$ (i.e. $H \cap S$, viewed inside $S$, is normal). Then there exist subgroups $P, I \le G$ with $H \le P \le I \le S$, both $P$ and $I$ normal in $S$ in the same sense, such that the index of $H$ in $P$ is $q^{n}$ for some natural number $n$; $q$ does not divide the index of $P$ in $I$; there is $g \in I$ such that every $s \in I$ satisfies $(g^{n})^{-1} s \in P$ for some natural number $n$; and there is $g \in S$ such that every $s \in S$ satisfies $(g^{n})^{-1} s \in I$ for some natural number $n$. The last two clauses express that $I/P$ and $S/I$ are cyclic, generated by the class of a single element with non-negative exponents.
--
--   This is the purely group-theoretic skeleton of the wild–tame–unramified filtration of the absolute Galois group of a $q$-adic field: $U$ plays the role of an open normal subgroup, $W$ of wild inertia times $U$, $t$ of a tame generator and $\varphi$ of a Frobenius lift, and the conclusion produces, inside any $S$ with normal subgroup $H \supseteq U$, a chain whose successive quotients are a $q$-group, a group of order prime to $q$ that is cyclic, and a cyclic group. It is used in the proof that Galois groups of finite extensions of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ are solvable ([`IntermediateField.isSolvable_algEquiv_of_padic`](thm.html#IntermediateField.isSolvable_algEquiv_of_padic)).
-- source:
